{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-124321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2v-u+2,\\,y=2u+v-5.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=-5$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2v-u+2 \\\\ 2u+v-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+2v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=(-1)\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2=-5.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d1f0ac8b187a9cd384a55943cf4866308f0013e03b0ac97a92f19502c17b300"} {"question" "q-124321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=4u-3v-5,\\,y=-2u+2v+4.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=2$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4u-3v-5 \\\\ -2u+2v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u-3v \\\\ -2u+2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|=4\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-2)=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $det(A)>0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d1f0ac8b187a9cd384a55943cf4866308f0013e03b0ac97a92f19502c17b300"} {"question" "q-124324" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124324" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124324" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/43eb119ef43e136682d4451e4f85f007c63568f7a34880c46f87ab45122f5dd0.png)\n\nConsider the rectangle $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=1-u,\\,y=2-v.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the image of $Δ$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-u \\\\ 2-v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u \\\\ -v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the boundary of $Δ$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $Δ,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/a8a13c579c3ca8cc32f997c48e237c38d449aa07040de658589fa5cc68a02c55.png)\n\n          \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our square:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(2,2),(-1,2),(-1,1),$ and $(2,1).$\n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/146f9f36deeac0f3a7108a173485eb6d0d03138d18998a96dc9c3566bee21ca2.png)\n\n          \n\nFinally, since $det(A)=1>0,$ this transformation is orientation-preserving." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d1f0ac8b187a9cd384a55943cf4866308f0013e03b0ac97a92f19502c17b300"} {"question" "q-124558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/01ddff6313a9f86ad9cb750a23f65900f7031afef2f30826efecba379064f3f7.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/4762d50ba86ed040fa1021afdedde9a7d23c873b2a8f5f434752f6e69af2bbb7.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/741501ec388180aca96136e286f1e871eeaa4e89c3ad36558fd5a384e6951001.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/93b061334bdf3b55345bd8e42bf9003f75d9f9221cd8b45d738f3c2bb1523d3a.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/c297c5a3c483cacf056d9765bca2e31d8056c157d334c2f1571e775cf671e579.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-124558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/741501ec388180aca96136e286f1e871eeaa4e89c3ad36558fd5a384e6951001.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-162188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=u+v-2,\\,y=u-3v+1.\n$$\n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-162188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v-2 \\\\ u-3v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 1=-4.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|-4|=4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-162188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d1f0ac8b187a9cd384a55943cf4866308f0013e03b0ac97a92f19502c17b300"} {"question" "q-162188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-162188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-162188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-162190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u-v,\\,y=2v-u-5.\n$$\n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-162190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ 2v-u-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ -u+2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-1)=3.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|3|=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-162190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d1f0ac8b187a9cd384a55943cf4866308f0013e03b0ac97a92f19502c17b300"} {"question" "q-162190" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-162190" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"} {"question" "q-162190" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e9a865273403918c5e5ef92c7b0510e17935f7b5a549c2287433faef953b52"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1875 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
